  "answer": "PEP 8 gives these guidelines for imports:\n\n- **Use separate lines** for imports such as `import os` and `import sys`. Importing multiple names from one module, such as `from subprocess import Popen, PIPE`, is fine. Put imports at the top of the file, after module comments and docstrings but before globals and constants; group them with standard-library imports first. [pep-0008/09-imports/0]\n- **Explicit relative imports are acceptable**, especially when absolute imports would be unnecessarily verbose in complex packages. Standard-library code should always use absolute imports. [pep-0008/09-imports/1]\n- **Avoid name clashes** by importing modules and using qualified names, such as `myclass.MyClass`. **Avoid wildcard imports** (`from module import *`), which obscure which names exist and confuse readers and automated tools. [pep-0008/09-imports/2]\n- **Treat imported names as implementation details**: other modules should not access them indirectly unless they are explicitly documented as part of the importing module\u2019s API. [pep-0008/34-public-and-internal-interfaces/1]",
